---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const updated = 'November 10, 2026';
---
<BaseLayout title="Terms of Service — SessionFS" description="The terms that apply when you use SessionFS: accounts, your content, acceptable use, plans and billing, and our responsibilities to each other.">
  <section class="relative pt-32 sm:pt-40 pb-20 px-5">
    <article class="legal max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
      <p class="meta">Last updated: {updated}</p>

      <p>These terms are an agreement between you and SessionFS ("SessionFS", "we", "us") for your use of the hosted SessionFS service: the dashboard at app.sessionfs.dev, the hosted API, and the accounts, sync, team and AI features they provide (the "Service"). By creating an account or using the Service, you agree to these terms and to our <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a>. If you use the Service on behalf of an organization, you agree for that organization and confirm you have authority to do so.</p>

      <h2>1. The software and the Service</h2>
      <p>The SessionFS software is open source. The core is licensed under the MIT License and the enterprise features under the Functional Source License; those licenses, not these terms, govern your use of the source code. You can use the <code>sfs</code> tool entirely on your own machine without an account. These terms apply when you create an account or use the hosted Service.</p>
      <p>If you have a separate signed agreement with us, such as an enterprise or self-hosted license, that agreement takes priority where it conflicts with these terms.</p>

      <h2>2. Your account</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>You must be at least 16 years old and able to form a binding contract.</li>
        <li>Give us accurate information and keep it up to date.</li>
        <li>Keep your API keys and sign-in methods secure. You are responsible for activity under your account and keys, including service keys you create for automated agents. Tell us promptly at <a href="mailto:security@sessionfs.dev">security@sessionfs.dev</a> if you think one has been compromised, and revoke it.</li>
        <li>Organization owners and admins control their organization's members, projects, keys and settings, and are responsible for their members' use of the Service.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>3. Your content</h2>
      <p>You own the content you put into the Service, including sessions, code, knowledge entries, tickets, transcripts and files ("Your Content"). You give us a limited license to host, copy, process, transmit and display Your Content only as needed to provide, secure and support the Service for you, and as you direct, for example when you share a session or hand it to a teammate. This license ends when Your Content is deleted from the Service, apart from short-lived backups.</p>
      <p>You are responsible for Your Content and confirm you have the rights to upload it. AI coding sessions can contain secrets, personal data and third parties' code. Review what you sync. The Service's secret scanning helps but does not guarantee that sensitive data is caught. Don't upload content you aren't allowed to share, and only upload meeting transcripts or chats you have the right to record and share.</p>

      <h2>4. AI features</h2>
      <p>AI features such as the session helper, security audits, summaries and action-item extraction run with an AI provider and key that you or your organization configure. Your use of that provider is also subject to its own terms, and you are responsible for any charges it bills you. AI output can be wrong or incomplete. Review it before you rely on it, especially for security findings, code and decisions.</p>

      <h2>5. Acceptable use</h2>
      <p>Don't use the Service to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>break the law or infringe anyone's rights;</li>
        <li>upload malware or content designed to harm others;</li>
        <li>access accounts, projects or data you aren't authorized to access;</li>
        <li>attack, overload or disrupt the Service, or get around rate limits, plan limits or security controls;</li>
        <li>publish skills or packages to the marketplace that are malicious, misleading or that you don't have the right to distribute;</li>
        <li>resell or provide the hosted Service to third parties as a service without our written agreement.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>We may remove content or restrict access that violates these terms.</p>

      <h2>6. Plans, billing and cancellation</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>The Free plan costs nothing. Paid plans are billed in advance, monthly or annually, through Stripe, and renew automatically until cancelled.</li>
        <li>You can cancel at any time. Cancellation takes effect at the end of the current billing period, and you keep paid features until then. Fees already paid are not refundable, except where the law requires a refund.</li>
        <li>Prices exclude taxes, which you are responsible for where they apply.</li>
        <li>We may change prices. We'll give you at least 30 days' notice before a change affects your next renewal.</li>
        <li>If a payment fails, we'll retry and tell you. If it still isn't paid, we may move your account to the Free plan. When an account moves to a lower plan, features of the higher plan stop working, but we don't delete your data because of the change, and you can still read and export it.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>7. Integrations and third-party services</h2>
      <p>The Service can connect to services you choose, such as GitHub, GitLab, Jira, Confluence and AI providers. Those services are run by others under their own terms. We aren't responsible for them, and a change on their side can affect an integration.</p>

      <h2>8. Feedback</h2>
      <p>If you send us ideas or feedback, we may use them without any obligation to you.</p>

      <h2>9. Suspension and termination</h2>
      <p>You can stop using the Service and close your account at any time. We may suspend or end your access if you seriously or repeatedly breach these terms, if we are required to by law, or if your use puts the Service or other users at risk. Where we reasonably can, we'll give notice first. After your account closes, you'll have 30 days to ask us for an export of Your Content; after that we delete it as described in the Privacy Policy. Sections 3 (ownership), 10, 11, 12 and 14 continue after termination.</p>

      <h2>10. Disclaimers</h2>
      <p>We work hard to keep the Service reliable and secure, but it is provided "as is" and "as available". To the extent the law allows, we disclaim all warranties, express or implied, including merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose and non-infringement, and we don't promise the Service will be uninterrupted or error-free. Keep your own copies of anything important; SessionFS keeps your sessions on your machine by default.</p>

      <h2>11. Limitation of liability</h2>
      <p>To the extent the law allows, neither party is liable for indirect, incidental, special, consequential or punitive damages, or for lost profits, revenue or data. Our total liability for any claim relating to the Service is limited to the greater of the amount you paid us in the 12 months before the claim and US $100. Nothing in these terms limits liability that cannot be limited by law.</p>

      <h2>12. Indemnity</h2>
      <p>If a third party makes a claim against us because of Your Content or your breach of these terms, you will cover our reasonable costs of defending it and any resulting damages.</p>

      <h2>13. Changes to these terms</h2>
      <p>We may update these terms. We'll post the new version here with a new date, and for significant changes we'll tell you by email or in the dashboard at least 14 days before they take effect. If you keep using the Service after a change takes effect, the new terms apply. If you don't agree, you can stop using the Service and close your account.</p>

      <h2>14. General</h2>
      <p>These terms are governed by the laws of the State of Maryland and the federal laws of the United States, without regard to conflict-of-law rules. Any dispute will be heard in the state or federal courts located in Maryland, and both parties agree to those courts' jurisdiction. If you are a consumer, you keep any protections that the law of the country where you live gives you. If any part of these terms can't be enforced, the rest still applies. If we don't enforce a term right away, we haven't waived it. You may not transfer these terms without our consent; we may transfer them as part of a merger, acquisition or sale of assets. These terms, the Privacy Policy and any separate agreement you sign with us are the whole agreement between you and us about the Service.</p>

      <h2>15. Contact</h2>
      <p>SessionFS<br />
      Legal: <a href="mailto:legal@sessionfs.dev">legal@sessionfs.dev</a><br />
      Support: <a href="mailto:support@sessionfs.dev">support@sessionfs.dev</a></p>
    </article>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .legal h1 { font-size: 2.25rem; line-height: 1.2; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: -0.02em; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }
  .legal .meta { color: var(--text-tertiary); font-size: 0.875rem; margin-bottom: 2rem; }
  .legal h2 { font-size: 1.375rem; line-height: 1.3; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: -0.01em; margin: 2.5rem 0 0.75rem; }
  .legal p, .legal li { line-height: 1.7; color: var(--text-secondary); }
  .legal p { margin-bottom: 1rem; }
  .legal ul { list-style: disc; padding-left: 1.4rem; margin-bottom: 1rem; }
  .legal li { margin-bottom: 0.4rem; }
  .legal a { color: var(--brand); text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 2px; }
  .legal code { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.9em; }
  .legal strong { color: var(--text-primary); }
</style>
